md`# brain-bluesky

A Cloud Brain channel: Bluesky messages to the Brain's own account arrive in the inbox, and answers go back with \`inbox.reply\`. A sender is their DID, so nobody links anything: the owner is answered from the first message, and anyone else once the owner has added their DID under People. In a group it answers the owner and people when they address it; see Groups.

| | |
|---|---|
| Worker | \`brain-x-bluesky\`, ticked once a minute |
| \`bluesky.send\` | procedure. The owner, a named token, or \`brain-x-inbox\` answering an entry; never a member. \`{ to, text }\` or \`{ to, image, text }\`; \`to\` is the owner's DID or a person's. With \`room\`, a group's conversation id, the text goes to that group, and \`to\` must be in it. |
| \`bluesky.poll\` | procedure, owner. Reads what is new now. The page calls it every 30 s while its tab answers. |
| \`bluesky.know\` | procedure, the kernel. \`{ address, forget }\` adds or drops one DID; \`{ all: [did] }\` replaces the set. |
| \`bluesky.room\` | procedure, the kernel. \`{ id }\` answers \`{ known, name, members, complete, served }\` for a group this Worker has seen, read from the chat service when what is kept is over 2 minutes old. |
| \`bluesky.start\` | procedure, owner. \`{ members, name, text }\`: makes a group of the owner and people already added (2 to 20 DIDs) and says \`text\` in it. \`{ id }\`. |
| \`bluesky.groups\` | query, owner. \`{ settings, groups }\`: each group \`{ id, name, people, complete, ownerIn, enabled, served, read }\`. |
| \`bluesky.group\` | procedure, owner. \`{ id, enabled }\` switches on a group the owner is not in. |
| \`bluesky.settings\` | procedure, owner. \`{ names, addressedOnly, groupInvites }\`: what the account answers to beside its handle, whether it answers only then, and who may add it to a group (\`all\`, \`following\`, \`none\`), which is written to the account at the next poll. |
| \`bluesky.putRecord\` | procedure. The owner in their tab, or \`brain-x-feed\` when the chain was started by the owner, in their tab or in a turn run for them (\`origin.kind == "owner"\`; *Origin* in \`@tomlarkworthy/brain-core\`). A token, or a member the owner gave \`feed.publish\`, does not write a record. Until 2026-10-08 the rule read \`origin.trusted\`, which let both through. \`{ collection, rkey, record }\` writes one record in the account's repo. \`collection\` must be \`app.bsky.feed.generator\`. \`{ did, handle, uri, cid }\`. |
| \`bluesky.deleteRecord\` | procedure, the same callers. \`{ collection, rkey }\` deletes that record. \`{ did, handle, uri }\`. |
| \`bluesky.status\` | query, owner. \`{ configured, handle, did, pds, signedIn, tick, lastPoll, lastError, backoffUntil, people, groups }\` |
| Secrets | \`BLUESKY_HANDLE\`, \`BLUESKY_APP_PASSWORD\`. Read from the core at most once in 5 minutes for one instance (\`config.credsMs\`), so a changed secret is followed within 5 minutes. |
| Settings | \`credsMs\` (300000): how long one instance keeps the two secrets. \`pollGapMs\` (3000): the least time between two reads of Bluesky. Changed with \`config.set\` on the core, no deploy. |
| Storage | \`rows\`: \`session\`, \`refused\`, \`cursor\`, \`since\`, \`known/<did>\`, \`convo/<did>\`, \`direct/<convo>\`, \`group/<convo>\`, \`heard/<convo>\`, \`settings\`, \`declared\`, \`declareError\`, \`accepted/<convo>\`, \`asked/<did>\`, \`asks\`, \`quiet/<did>\`, \`polled\`, \`tick\`, \`busy\`, \`backoff\`, \`error\` |

With either secret unset, a tick writes \`tick\` and stops: no request leaves the Worker, and \`bluesky.status\` answers \`{ configured: false }\`.`
// %%
viewof blueskyStatus = {
  const out = html`<div style="font: 13px var(--sans-serif, system-ui)"></div>`;
  const when = (t) => (t ? new Date(t).toLocaleTimeString() : "never");
  const read = async () => {
    try {
      const s = await client.query("bluesky.status");
      out.value = s;
      out.textContent = !s.configured
        ? "Bluesky: not configured."
        : `Bluesky: ${s.signedIn ? "signed in as @" + s.handle : "not signed in"}; last poll ${when(s.lastPoll && s.lastPoll.at)}${s.lastError ? "; error at " + when(s.lastError.at) + ": " + s.lastError.message : ""}${s.backoffUntil ? "; waiting until " + when(s.backoffUntil) : ""}`;
    } catch (e) {
      out.value = null;
      out.textContent = "Bluesky: " + String((e && e.message) || e);
    }
  };
  const check = Inputs.button("Check", { reduce: read });
  if (session && session.owner) read();
  else out.textContent = "Bluesky: sign in as the owner to see its state.";
  return Object.assign(html`<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center">${check}${out}</div>`, { value: null });
}
// %%
bluesky_setup = md`## Setting up

1. Make a Bluesky account for the Brain at [bsky.app](https://bsky.app). It asks for a phone number, which is why this Worker cannot make it.
2. In that account: Settings → Privacy and security → App passwords → Add, and tick **Allow access to your direct messages**.
3. In the Cloud Brain notebook set two secrets, each with the rule \`caller.worker in ["brain-x-bluesky"]\`: \`BLUESKY_HANDLE\` (\`name.bsky.social\`) and \`BLUESKY_APP_PASSWORD\`.
4. Press Check above within two minutes. It reads "signed in as @name".
5. From your own account, send the Brain's account a message.

The Worker writes the account's \`chat.bsky.actor.declaration\` at its first poll after signing in: \`allowIncoming: "all"\`, where a new account takes messages only from accounts it follows, and \`allowGroupInvites: "all"\`, which read \`"none"\` on this account on 2026-10-07. Who may add it to a group is a setting under Groups. People added before this Worker was deployed are known to it from the next change under People.`
// %%
md`## What it calls

Each was read from the lexicons in [bluesky-social/atproto](https://github.com/bluesky-social/atproto/tree/main/lexicons) at \`d29d7ab\` on 2026-10-07, and none has been called with a real account yet.

| | |
|---|---|
| Where | The account's own PDS, found from the handle (\`com.atproto.identity.resolveHandle\` on \`public.api.bsky.app\`, then the DID document). Chat calls carry \`atproto-proxy: did:web:api.bsky.chat#bsky_chat\`. |
| Sign-in | \`com.atproto.server.createSession\`, then \`refreshSession\` 5 minutes before the access token ends or when a call answers 401 or \`ExpiredToken\`. A refused password is tried again after 10 minutes, or at once when either secret changes. |
| Reading | \`chat.bsky.convo.getLog\` with the stored cursor, up to 5 pages a poll. It is one call for every conversation, where \`listConvos\` and \`getMessages\` are one call and then one per conversation with something unread. |
| Whose | \`chat.bsky.convo.getConvo\`, once per conversation, says direct or group. For a group, \`getConvoMembers\`, 100 a page and 3 pages at most: \`convoView.members\` holds "the first few members" and not the list. |
| Writing | \`chat.bsky.convo.sendMessage\`, then \`updateRead\`. \`acceptConvo\` once per person. |

A message is at most 1000 graphemes and 10000 bytes (\`chat.bsky.convo.defs#messageInput\`); a longer answer is sent as several, cut at a paragraph, a line or a space, 10 at most. A message can embed a post and nothing else, so **no picture travels in either direction**: \`image\` is sent as its address after the text, and a post somebody shares arrives as \`[post: at://…]\`. Addresses in a reply are marked as links.

Messages sent more than 10 minutes before the first sign-in are not read. A 429 stops every call until the time in its \`ratelimit-reset\` header, or for 1, 2, 4 … 60 minutes without one.

A DID the owner has not added gets one answer an hour, 20 an hour over all DIDs, and no entry.`
// %%
md`## Groups

A reply in a group is read by everyone in it, and a turn runs with its sender's permissions. So:

| | |
|---|---|
| Which groups | One the owner is in, or one the owner has switched on below. A message in any other group is dropped. Anyone may add the account to a group unless "Who may add it" says otherwise. |
| Whose messages | The owner's and people's. Anyone else in the group gets no answer and no notice. |
| Which messages | One that mentions the account (a \`#mention\` facet with its DID), replies to one of its messages (\`replyTo.sender\`), or begins with its handle or a name set below. With "Only when addressed" off, every message from the owner or a person. |
| The rest | Kept in \`heard/<convo>\`, the last 20 at 500 characters each, and sent with the next entry as \`body.heard\`, so the assistant has what was said. Messages from people who are not members are in it. Only what somebody who is in the group when the entry is made said is sent: what a person said before they left or were removed is dropped then. Past 300 members the list is not whole, and what somebody outside it said is dropped too. |
| The entry | \`body.room: { id, name, members, complete }\`: every DID in the group but the account's own, read from the chat service when the entry is made. \`complete\` is false past 300 members. |
| The reply | \`inbox.reply\` passes the entry's \`room.id\` to \`bluesky.send\`, which writes to that conversation. |

What a turn in a group may call is decided by the kernel from who is in the room, not here; see \`@tomlarkworthy/brain-kernel\`, "Rooms". The kernel asks \`bluesky.room\` for the members again when it hands out the turn. A join, a leave or a rename in the log (\`logAddMember\`, \`logRemoveMember\`, \`logMemberJoin\`, \`logMemberLeave\`, \`logEditGroup\`) marks what is kept as stale.

Not sent to a group: the "not one of them" answer to a stranger, and the "No Brain tab is open" notice.

Read from the lexicons at \`d29d7ab\` on 2026-10-07 and not yet called with a real account: \`groupConvo\`, \`getConvoMembers\`, \`replyTo\`, the five log events.`
// %%
viewof blueskyGroups = {
  const out = html`<div></div>`;
  const on = (input, send) => (input.addEventListener("input", () => send(input.value).then(draw, (e) => (out.textContent = String((e && e.message) || e)))), input);
  const draw = async () => {
    try {
      const { groups, settings } = await client.query("bluesky.groups");
      out.replaceChildren(
        on(Inputs.toggle({ label: "Only when addressed", value: settings.addressedOnly }), (v) => client.procedure("bluesky.settings", { addressedOnly: v })),
        on(Inputs.select(["all", "following", "none"], { label: "Who may add it to a group", value: settings.groupInvites }), (v) => client.procedure("bluesky.settings", { groupInvites: v })),
        on(Inputs.text({ label: "Also answers to", value: settings.names.join(", "), placeholder: "brain, bot", submit: "Save" }), (v) => client.procedure("bluesky.settings", { names: v.split(",") })),
        ...groups.map((g) => on(Inputs.toggle({ label: `${g.name || g.id}: ${g.people.slice(0, 8).join(", ")}${g.people.length > 8 || !g.complete ? " …" : ""}${g.ownerIn ? " (you are in it)" : ""}`, value: g.served, disabled: g.ownerIn }), (v) => client.procedure("bluesky.group", { id: g.id, enabled: v }))),
        ...(groups.length ? [] : [html`<i>No group has been seen.</i>`])
      );
    } catch (e) {
      out.textContent = "Groups: " + String((e && e.message) || e);
    }
  };
  if (session && session.owner) draw();
  else out.textContent = "Groups: sign in as the owner.";
  return Object.assign(html`<div>${Inputs.button("Refresh groups", { reduce: draw })}${out}</div>`, { value: null });
}
// %%
// A reply as the messages that carry it: each at most `max` graphemes and `maxBytes` of UTF-8, cut at a
// paragraph, a line or a space when one falls in the second half of what fits.
blueskySplit = (text, max = 1000, maxBytes = 10000) => {
  const segmenter = new Intl.Segmenter(undefined, { granularity: "grapheme" }), encoder = new TextEncoder();
  const out = [];
  let rest = String(text).trim();
  while (rest) {
    let piece = "", n = 0, size = 0, first = null;
    for (const { segment } of segmenter.segment(rest)) {
      first ??= segment;
      const b = encoder.encode(segment).length;
      if (n === max || size + b > maxBytes) break;
      piece += segment;
      n++;
      size += b;
    }
    // One grapheme larger than a whole message cannot be sent.
    if (!piece) {
      rest = rest.slice(first.length).trimStart();
      continue;
    }
    if (piece.length < rest.length)
      for (const gap of ["\n\n", "\n", " "]) {
        const at = piece.lastIndexOf(gap);
        if (at > piece.length / 2) {
          piece = piece.slice(0, at);
          break;
        }
      }
    out.push(piece.trimEnd());
    rest = rest.slice(piece.length).trimStart();
  }
  return out;
}
// %%
// app.bsky.richtext.facet links for the addresses in a message. A client shows no link without one.
blueskyFacets = (text) => {
  const encoder = new TextEncoder();
  return [...text.matchAll(/https?:\/\/[^\s<>"]+/g)].map((m) => {
    const uri = m[0].replace(/[.,;:!?)\]]+$/, ""), byteStart = encoder.encode(text.slice(0, m.index)).length;
    return { index: { byteStart, byteEnd: byteStart + encoder.encode(uri).length }, features: [{ $type: "app.bsky.richtext.facet#link", uri }] };
  });
}
// %%
blueskyOps = {
  const HOUR = 3600000, CHAT = "did:web:api.bsky.chat#bsky_chat", NS = "chat.bsky.convo.";
  const stop = (code, message) => Object.assign(new Error(message), { code });
  const expiry = (jwt) => {
    try {
      return JSON.parse(atob(String(jwt).split(".")[1].replace(/-/g, "+").replace(/_/g, "/"))).exp * 1000 || 0;
    } catch {
      return 0;
    }
  };
  // The two secrets are kept in this instance for credsMs: each read is a call to the core, and a poll made two.
  // A changed secret is followed within that time. A missing one is not kept.
  let kept = null;
  const creds = async () => {
    const ms = config.credsMs ?? 300000;
    if (ms > 0 && kept && Date.now() - kept.at < ms) return kept.c;
    const handle = await secrets.BLUESKY_HANDLE, password = await secrets.BLUESKY_APP_PASSWORD;
    if (!handle || !password) return (kept = null);
    const c = { handle: String(handle).trim().replace(/^@/, ""), password: String(password).trim() };
    // Says whether the secrets are the ones a session or a refusal was made with.
    const out = { ...c, mark: (await sha256(c.handle + "\n" + c.password)).slice(0, 16) };
    if (ms > 0) kept = { at: Date.now(), c: out };
    return out;
  };
  const call = async (url, init) => {
    const r = await fetch(url, init);
    const data = await r.json().catch(() => null);
    if (r.status === 429) {
      const was = (await rows.get("backoff")) || { step: 0 }, now = Date.now(), reset = Number(r.headers.get("ratelimit-reset")) * 1000;
      await rows.put("backoff", { until: now + Math.min(reset > now ? reset - now : 60000 * 2 ** was.step, HOUR), step: was.step + 1 });
      throw stop("limited", "429 from " + new URL(url).hostname);
    }
    return { ok: r.ok, status: r.status, data };
  };
  const said = (what, r) => `${what}: ${r.status} ${(r.data && r.data.error) || ""} ${(r.data && r.data.message) || ""}`.trim().slice(0, 300);
  const json = (body, headers = {}) => ({ method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json", ...headers }, body: JSON.stringify(body) });
  const blocked = async () => {
    const b = await rows.get("backoff");
    return b && b.until > Date.now() ? b.until : 0;
  };

  const settings = async () => ({ names: [], addressedOnly: true, groupInvites: "all", ...((await rows.get("settings")) || {}) });
  const pdsOf = async (handle) => {
    const did = handle.startsWith("did:") ? handle : ((await call("https://public.api.bsky.app/xrpc/com.atproto.identity.resolveHandle?handle=" + encodeURIComponent(handle))).data || {}).did;
    if (!/^did:(plc|web):[A-Za-z0-9.:%-]+$/.test(did || "")) throw stop("identity", `${handle} does not resolve to a DID`);
    const doc = (await call(did.startsWith("did:plc:") ? "https://plc.directory/" + did : `https://${decodeURIComponent(did.slice("did:web:".length).split(":")[0])}/.well-known/did.json`)).data;
    const pds = ((doc && doc.service) || []).find((s) => String(s.id).endsWith("#atproto_pds"));
    if (!pds || !/^https:\/\/[^/]+\/?$/.test(pds.serviceEndpoint || "")) throw stop("identity", `${did} names no PDS`);
    return { did, pds: pds.serviceEndpoint.replace(/\/$/, "") };
  };
  const signIn = async (c) => {
    const refused = await rows.get("refused");
    if (refused && refused.mark === c.mark && Date.now() - refused.at < 600000) throw stop("refused", refused.message);
    const { did, pds } = await pdsOf(c.handle);
    const r = await call(pds + "/xrpc/com.atproto.server.createSession", json({ identifier: c.handle, password: c.password }));
    if (!r.ok || !r.data || r.data.did !== did) {
      const message = r.ok ? "the PDS signed in another account" : said("createSession", r);
      await rows.put("refused", { mark: c.mark, at: Date.now(), message });
      throw stop("refused", message);
    }
    const was = await rows.get("session"), s = { did, handle: c.handle, mark: c.mark, pds, accessJwt: r.data.accessJwt, refreshJwt: r.data.refreshJwt, at: Date.now() };
    // Another account: nothing kept about the last one's conversations applies.
    if (was && was.did !== did) for (const key of ["cursor", "since", "convo/", "direct/", "accepted/", "group/", "heard/"]) await rows.deletePrefix(key);
    await rows.put("session", s);
    await rows.delete("refused");
    if (!(await rows.get("since"))) await rows.put("since", Date.now() - 600000);
    await rows.delete("declared");
    return s;
  };
  // The account's chat.bsky.actor.declaration. A new account takes messages only from accounts it follows, and
  // cosmiccalendrics read allowGroupInvites: "none" on 2026-10-07: nobody could add it to a group.
  // Written when what `declared` remembers is not what is wanted: after a sign-in, and when the setting changes.
  const declare = async (s) => {
    const want = { allowIncoming: "all", allowGroupInvites: (await settings()).groupInvites }, mark = want.allowIncoming + "/" + want.allowGroupInvites;
    if ((await rows.get("declared")) === mark) return;
    const at = `repo=${encodeURIComponent(s.did)}&collection=chat.bsky.actor.declaration&rkey=self`, auth = { authorization: "Bearer " + s.accessJwt };
    const now = await call(`${s.pds}/xrpc/com.atproto.repo.getRecord?${at}`, { headers: auth }), value = (now.ok && now.data && now.data.value) || {};
    if (value.allowIncoming !== want.allowIncoming || value.allowGroupInvites !== want.allowGroupInvites) {
      const put = await call(s.pds + "/xrpc/com.atproto.repo.putRecord", json({ repo: s.did, collection: "chat.bsky.actor.declaration", rkey: "self", record: { ...value, $type: "chat.bsky.actor.declaration", ...want } }, auth));
      if (!put.ok) return void (await rows.put("declareError", { at: Date.now(), message: said("could not write chat.bsky.actor.declaration", put) }));
    }
    await rows.delete("declareError");
    await rows.put("declared", mark);
  };
  const refresh = async (s, c) => {
    const r = await call(s.pds + "/xrpc/com.atproto.server.refreshSession", { method: "POST", headers: { authorization: "Bearer " + s.refreshJwt } });
    if (!r.ok || !r.data || !r.data.accessJwt) {
      await rows.delete("session");
      return signIn(c);
    }
    const next = { ...s, accessJwt: r.data.accessJwt, refreshJwt: r.data.refreshJwt, at: Date.now() };
    await rows.put("session", next);
    return next;
  };
  const sessionFor = async (c) => {
    const s = await rows.get("session");
    if (!s || s.mark !== c.mark) return signIn(c);
    const ends = expiry(s.accessJwt);
    return ends && ends - Date.now() < 300000 ? refresh(s, c) : s;
  };
  // One chat method, on the PDS, as the account. `body` makes it a procedure.
  const chat = async (c, name, { params = {}, body } = {}) => {
    const query = new URLSearchParams();
    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(params)) for (const x of [].concat(v)) query.append(k, x);
    const go = (s) => call(`${s.pds}/xrpc/${name.includes(".") ? "chat.bsky." : NS}${name}${[...query].length ? "?" + query : ""}`, body ? json(body, { authorization: "Bearer " + s.accessJwt, "atproto-proxy": CHAT }) : { headers: { authorization: "Bearer " + s.accessJwt, "atproto-proxy": CHAT } });
    let s = await sessionFor(c), r = await go(s);
    if (r.status === 401 || (r.data && r.data.error === "ExpiredToken")) r = await go(await refresh(s, c));
    if (!r.ok) throw stop("upstream", said(name, r));
    return r.data || {};
  };
  const say = async (c, convoId, text) => {
    for (const part of blueskySplit(text).slice(0, 10)) {
      const facets = blueskyFacets(part);
      await chat(c, "sendMessage", { body: { convoId, message: facets.length ? { text: part, facets } : { text: part } } });
    }
  };
  // A group is read and written when the owner is in it or has switched it on.
  const servedGroup = (g) => !!g && (!!g.enabled || (!!config.owner && g.members.includes(config.owner)));
  // Everyone in a group but the account itself. convoView.members names only a few of them, so this pages
  // getConvoMembers: 300 at most, and `complete` says whether that was all.
  const readGroup = async (c, s, convoId, convo) => {
    const members = [], handles = {};
    let cursor, complete = false;
    for (let page = 0; page < 3 && !complete; page++) {
      const r = await chat(c, "getConvoMembers", { params: { convoId, limit: 100, ...(cursor ? { cursor } : {}) } });
      for (const m of r.members || []) {
        if (m.did === s.did || /#pastGroupConvoMember$/.test((m.kind && m.kind.$type) || "")) continue;
        members.push(m.did);
        handles[m.did] = m.handle || null;
      }
      cursor = r.cursor;
      complete = !cursor || !(r.members || []).length;
    }
    const was = (await rows.get("group/" + convoId)) || {};
    const g = { id: convoId, name: String((convo && convo.kind && convo.kind.name) || "").slice(0, 100), members, handles, complete, at: Date.now(), enabled: !!was.enabled };
    await rows.put("group/" + convoId, g);
    return g;
  };
  // What a conversation is: { direct: did } or { group }. A direct one never changes. A group's members are
  // read again when what is kept is older than maxAge, or when the log said somebody joined or left.
  const where = async (c, s, convoId, maxAge = 120000) => {
    const d = await rows.get("direct/" + convoId);
    if (d && d.with) return { direct: d.with };
    const g = await rows.get("group/" + convoId);
    if (g && Date.now() - g.at < maxAge) return { group: g };
    const { convo } = await chat(c, "getConvo", { params: { convoId } });
    const listed = ((convo && convo.members) || []).map((m) => m.did), kind = convo && convo.kind && convo.kind.$type;
    if (kind ? kind === "chat.bsky.convo.defs#directConvo" : listed.length === 2) {
      const other = listed.find((m) => m !== s.did) || null;
      if (other) {
        await rows.put("direct/" + convoId, { with: other });
        await rows.put("convo/" + other, convoId);
      }
      return { direct: other };
    }
    return { group: await readGroup(c, s, convoId, convo) };
  };
  const served = async (did) => (!!config.owner && did === config.owner) || !!(await rows.get("known/" + did));
  // In a group the account answers what is said to it: a mention of it, a reply to one of its own messages,
  // or a message that begins with its handle or one of the owner's names for it.
  const addressed = (m, s, names) => {
    if ((m.facets || []).some((f) => (f.features || []).some((x) => x.$type === "app.bsky.richtext.facet#mention" && x.did === s.did))) return true;
    if (m.replyTo && m.replyTo.sender && m.replyTo.sender.did === s.did) return true;
    const text = String(m.text || "").trim().toLowerCase();
    return [s.handle, ...names].some((n) => {
      n = String(n || "").trim().toLowerCase().replace(/^@/, "");
      const rest = n && (text.startsWith("@" + n) ? text.slice(n.length + 1) : text.startsWith(n) ? text.slice(n.length) : null);
      return rest != null && !/^[a-z0-9_.-]*[a-z0-9_]/.test(rest);
    });
  };
  const textOf = (m) => {
    const post = m.embed && m.embed.record && m.embed.record.uri;
    return [m.text, post ? `[post: ${post}]` : ""].filter(Boolean).join("\n");
  };
  // A message in a group. Said to the account by the owner or a person: an entry, carrying who is in the room
  // and what was said there since the last one. Anything else in a group that is served: kept, 20 messages at most.
  const takeGroup = async (c, s, log, g, known, now) => {
    const m = log.message, from = m.sender.did, id = log.convoId, set = await settings();
    if (!servedGroup(g)) return;
    if (!known || (set.addressedOnly && !addressed(m, s, set.names))) {
      const heard = (await rows.get("heard/" + id)) || [];
      await rows.put("heard/" + id, [...heard, { from, handle: g.handles[from] || null, text: textOf(m).slice(0, 500), at: Date.parse(m.sentAt) || now }].slice(-20));
      return;
    }
    // Who is in the room is read now, not taken from what was kept.
    if (now - g.at > 5000) g = (await where(c, s, id, 0)).group;
    if (!g || !servedGroup(g) || !g.members.includes(from)) return;
    if (await rows.putIfAbsent("accepted/" + id, now)) await chat(c, "acceptConvo", { body: { convoId: id } }).catch(() => null);
    // Only what somebody who is in the room now said. What a person said before they left or were removed goes with the row.
    const heard = ((await rows.get("heard/" + id)) || []).filter((h) => g.members.includes(h.from));
    await inbox.append({ source: "bluesky", key: "bsky:" + m.id, body: { text: textOf(m), address: from, at: Date.parse(m.sentAt) || now, room: { id, name: g.name, members: g.members, complete: g.complete }, ...(heard.length ? { heard } : {}) } });
    await rows.delete("heard/" + id);
  };

  const take = async (c, s, log, since, now, taken) => {
    const m = log.message, kind = String(log.$type || "").replace("chat.bsky.convo.defs#log", "");
    // Somebody joined or left a group, or it was renamed: what is kept about it is read again before it is used.
    if (["AddMember", "RemoveMember", "MemberJoin", "MemberLeave", "EditGroup"].includes(kind)) {
      const g = await rows.get("group/" + log.convoId);
      if (g) await rows.put("group/" + log.convoId, { ...g, at: 0 });
      return;
    }
    if (kind === "LeaveConvo") {
      await rows.delete("group/" + log.convoId);
      await rows.delete("heard/" + log.convoId);
      return;
    }
    if (kind !== "CreateMessage" || !m || m.$type !== "chat.bsky.convo.defs#messageView" || !m.sender) return;
    const from = m.sender.did, at = Date.parse(m.sentAt) || now;
    if (from === s.did || at < since) return;
    if (await served(from)) {
      const w = await where(c, s, log.convoId);
      if (w.group) return takeGroup(c, s, log, w.group, true, now);
      if (w.direct !== from) return;
      if (await rows.putIfAbsent("accepted/" + log.convoId, now)) await chat(c, "acceptConvo", { body: { convoId: log.convoId } }).catch(() => null);
      await inbox.append({ source: "bluesky", key: "bsky:" + m.id, body: { text: textOf(m), address: from, at } });
      taken.push(from);
      return;
    }
    // A DID the owner has not added. In a group already read: kept as what was said there, and never answered.
    const group = await rows.get("group/" + log.convoId);
    if (group) return takeGroup(c, s, log, group, false, now);
    // Otherwise no entry, and one answer within the two limits, in a direct conversation only.
    if (now - ((await rows.get("asked/" + from)) || 0) < HOUR) return;
    const asks = (await rows.get("asks")) || { from: 0, n: 0 };
    const window = now - asks.from < HOUR ? asks : { from: now, n: 0 };
    if (window.n >= 20 || (await where(c, s, log.convoId)).direct !== from) return;
    await rows.put("asks", { from: window.from, n: window.n + 1 });
    await rows.put("asked/" + from, now);
    await say(c, log.convoId, `This account answers people its owner has added, and ${from} is not one of them.`);
  };

  const poll = async (by) => {
    const c = await creds();
    if (!c) return { configured: false };
    const now = Date.now(), until = await blocked(), last = await rows.get("polled"), busy = await rows.get("busy");
    // One poll at a time: the tick and a tab's call would otherwise answer the same stranger twice.
    if (until) return { configured: true, skipped: "backing off", until };
    if (last && now - last.at < (config.pollGapMs ?? 3000)) return { configured: true, skipped: "polled " + (now - last.at) + " ms ago" };
    if (busy && now - busy >= 60000) await rows.delete("busy");
    if (!(await rows.putIfAbsent("busy", now))) return { configured: true, skipped: "a poll is running" };
    const taken = [];
    let events = 0;
    try {
      const s = await sessionFor(c), since = (await rows.get("since")) || 0;
      await declare(s);
      for (let page = 0; page < 5; page++) {
        const cursor = await rows.get("cursor");
        const r = await chat(c, "getLog", { params: cursor ? { cursor } : {} });
        for (const log of r.logs || []) await take(c, s, log, since, now, taken);
        events += (r.logs || []).length;
        // Kept once the page is in the inbox. A page read twice appends nothing twice: the inbox keeps a key once.
        if (r.cursor && r.cursor !== cursor) await rows.put("cursor", r.cursor);
        if (!(r.logs || []).length || !r.cursor || r.cursor === cursor) break;
      }
      if (taken.length) {
        // No tab is answering: say so, to each person at most once an hour.
        const { held } = await xrpc.query("com.lopecode.brain.lease.get", {});
        for (const did of held ? [] : new Set(taken)) {
          if (now - ((await rows.get("quiet/" + did)) || 0) <= HOUR) continue;
          await rows.put("quiet/" + did, now);
          await say(c, await rows.get("convo/" + did), `No Brain tab is open, so this waits until one is. https://${config.host}/`);
        }
      }
      await rows.put("polled", { at: Date.now(), by, events, taken: taken.length });
      await rows.delete("backoff");
      await rows.delete("error");
      return { configured: true, events, taken: taken.length };
    } catch (e) {
      const message = String((e && e.message) || e).slice(0, 300);
      await rows.put("error", { at: Date.now(), message });
      return { configured: true, error: message };
    } finally {
      await rows.delete("busy");
    }
  };

  return {
    poll,
    tick: async () => {
      await rows.put("tick", Date.now());
      return poll("tick");
    },
    send: async ({ to, text, room }) => {
      const c = await creds();
      if (!c) throw stop("unconfigured", "BLUESKY_HANDLE and BLUESKY_APP_PASSWORD are not set");
      if (!(await served(to))) throw stop("forbidden", "bluesky.send writes to the owner and to people only");
      if (await blocked()) throw stop("limited", "backing off after a 429");
      if (room != null) {
        // An answer to a message from a group goes to that group, which everyone in it reads.
        const g = await rows.get("group/" + room);
        if (!servedGroup(g) || !g.members.includes(to)) throw stop("forbidden", "bluesky.send writes to a group the owner is in or has switched on, for a person in it");
        await say(c, room, text);
        await chat(c, "updateRead", { body: { convoId: room } }).catch(() => null);
        return;
      }
      let convoId = await rows.get("convo/" + to);
      if (!convoId) {
        convoId = (await chat(c, "getConvoForMembers", { params: { members: [to] } })).convo.id;
        await rows.put("convo/" + to, convoId);
      }
      await say(c, convoId, text);
      await chat(c, "updateRead", { body: { convoId } }).catch(() => null);
    },
    know: async ({ address, forget, all }) => {
      if (Array.isArray(all)) {
        const now = new Set(all.filter((d) => typeof d === "string" && d));
        for (const { key } of await rows.list("known/")) if (!now.has(key.slice("known/".length))) await rows.delete(key);
        for (const did of now) await rows.putIfAbsent("known/" + did, { at: Date.now() });
        return { known: now.size };
      }
      if (forget) await rows.delete("known/" + address);
      else await rows.put("known/" + address, { at: Date.now() });
      return { known: !forget };
    },
    // Who is in a group now, for the kernel, which asks when it hands out a turn.
    room: async ({ id }) => {
      const c = await creds();
      if (!c || !(await rows.get("group/" + id))) return { id, known: false };
      const g = (await where(c, await sessionFor(c), id)).group;
      return g ? { id, known: true, name: g.name, members: g.members, complete: g.complete, served: servedGroup(g) } : { id, known: false };
    },
    groups: async () => ({
      settings: await settings(),
      groups: (await rows.list("group/")).map(({ value: g }) => ({ id: g.id, name: g.name, people: g.members.map((d) => g.handles[d] || d), complete: g.complete, ownerIn: !!config.owner && g.members.includes(config.owner), enabled: !!g.enabled, served: servedGroup(g), read: g.at }))
    }),
    // The owner starts a group: themselves and people already added, so it is one the Worker serves.
    start: async ({ members, name, text }) => {
      const c = await creds();
      if (!c) throw stop("unconfigured", "BLUESKY_HANDLE and BLUESKY_APP_PASSWORD are not set");
      if (!config.owner || !members.includes(config.owner)) throw stop("forbidden", "bluesky.start makes a group the owner is in");
      for (const did of members) if (!(await served(did))) throw stop("forbidden", "bluesky.start invites the owner and people only");
      if (await blocked()) throw stop("limited", "backing off after a 429");
      const id = (await chat(c, "group.createGroup", { body: { members, name } })).convo.id;
      if (text) await say(c, id, text);
      return { id };
    },
    // One record in the account's own repo: written, or deleted when `record` is absent.
    record: async ({ collection, rkey, record }) => {
      const c = await creds();
      if (!c) throw stop("unconfigured", "BLUESKY_HANDLE and BLUESKY_APP_PASSWORD are not set");
      if (await blocked()) throw stop("limited", "backing off after a 429");
      const go = (s) => call(`${s.pds}/xrpc/com.atproto.repo.${record ? "putRecord" : "deleteRecord"}`, json({ repo: s.did, collection, rkey, ...(record ? { record: { ...record, $type: collection } } : {}) }, { authorization: "Bearer " + s.accessJwt }));
      let s = await sessionFor(c), r = await go(s);
      if (r.status === 401 || (r.data && r.data.error === "ExpiredToken")) r = await go((s = await refresh(s, c)));
      if (!r.ok) throw stop("upstream", said(record ? "putRecord" : "deleteRecord", r));
      return { did: s.did, handle: s.handle, uri: `at://${s.did}/${collection}/${rkey}`, ...(record ? { cid: (r.data && r.data.cid) || null } : {}) };
    },
    group: async ({ id, enabled }) => {
      const g = await rows.get("group/" + id);
      if (!g) throw stop("missing", "no group " + String(id).slice(0, 80));
      await rows.put("group/" + id, { ...g, enabled: !!enabled });
      return { id, enabled: !!enabled };
    },
    settings: async ({ names, addressedOnly, groupInvites }) => {
      const now = await settings();
      if (Array.isArray(names)) now.names = names.filter((n) => typeof n === "string" && n.trim()).map((n) => n.trim().slice(0, 40)).slice(0, 10);
      if (typeof addressedOnly === "boolean") now.addressedOnly = addressedOnly;
      if (["all", "following", "none"].includes(groupInvites)) now.groupInvites = groupInvites;
      await rows.put("settings", now);
      return now;
    },
    status: async () => {
      const c = await creds(), s = await rows.get("session");
      const live = !!(c && s && s.mark === c.mark);
      return { configured: !!c, handle: c ? c.handle : null, did: live ? s.did : null, pds: live ? s.pds : null, signedIn: live, tick: await rows.get("tick"), lastPoll: await rows.get("polled"), lastError: (await rows.get("error")) || (await rows.get("refused")) || (await rows.get("declareError")) || null, backoffUntil: (await blocked()) || null, people: (await rows.list("known/")).length, groups: (await rows.list("group/")).length };
    }
  };
}
// %%
blueskyApp = {
  const app = new hono.Hono();
  const NS = "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.";
  const fail = (c, status, error, message) => c.json({ error, message }, status);
  const STATUS = { limited: [429, "RateLimitExceeded"], unconfigured: [503, "NotConfigured"], forbidden: [403, "Forbidden"], missing: [404, "NotFound"] };
  app.onError((e, c) => fail(c, ...(STATUS[e && e.code] || [e && e.code ? 502 : 500, e && e.code ? "UpstreamError" : "InternalServerError"]), String((e && e.message) || e)));
  // The core has named the caller and checked it against the method's rule.
  const kernel = async (c, next) => (c.req.header("x-brain-caller") === "kernel" ? next() : fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the kernel"));
  app.post(NS + "send", async (c) => {
    const { to, text, image, room } = await c.req.json();
    if (image != null && (typeof image !== "string" || image.length > 2000 || !/^https:\/\//.test(image))) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "image must be an https URL");
    const whole = [typeof text === "string" ? text.trim() : "", image || ""].filter(Boolean).join("\n");
    if (!whole) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "text");
    if (typeof to !== "string") return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", "bluesky.send writes to the owner and to people only");
    if (room != null && (typeof room !== "string" || !room || room.length > 200)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "room");
    await blueskyOps.send({ to, text: whole, room });
    return c.json({ sent: true });
  });
  app.post(NS + "room", kernel, async (c) => {
    const { id } = await c.req.json();
    if (typeof id !== "string" || !id || id.length > 200) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "id");
    return c.json(await blueskyOps.room({ id }));
  });
  app.post(NS + "start", async (c) => {
    const { members, name, text } = await c.req.json();
    if (!Array.isArray(members) || members.length < 2 || members.length > 20 || !members.every((d) => typeof d === "string" && /^did:[a-z]+:[\w.:%-]{1,200}$/.test(d))) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "members: 2 to 20 DIDs");
    if (typeof name !== "string" || !name.trim() || [...name].length > 50) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "name: 1 to 50 characters");
    if (text != null && (typeof text !== "string" || text.length > 4096)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "text");
    return c.json(await blueskyOps.start({ members: [...new Set(members)], name: name.trim(), text: text && text.trim() }));
  });
  // The collections another service may write in the account's repo. A record of any other collection is refused.
  const RECORDS = ["app.bsky.feed.generator"];
  for (const name of ["putRecord", "deleteRecord"])
    app.post(NS + name, async (c) => {
      const { collection, rkey, record } = await c.req.json();
      if (!RECORDS.includes(collection)) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `bluesky.${name} writes ${RECORDS.join(", ")} only`);
      if (typeof rkey !== "string" || !/^[A-Za-z0-9._~-]{1,80}$/.test(rkey) || /^\.+$/.test(rkey)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "rkey");
      if (name === "putRecord" && (!record || typeof record !== "object" || Array.isArray(record) || JSON.stringify(record).length > 20000)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "record");
      return c.json(await blueskyOps.record({ collection, rkey, record: name === "putRecord" ? record : null }));
    });
  app.get(NS + "groups", async (c) => c.json(await blueskyOps.groups()));
  app.post(NS + "group", async (c) => {
    const { id, enabled } = await c.req.json();
    if (typeof id !== "string" || typeof enabled !== "boolean") return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "id and enabled");
    return c.json(await blueskyOps.group({ id, enabled }));
  });
  app.post(NS + "settings", async (c) => c.json(await blueskyOps.settings(await c.req.json())));
  app.post(NS + "poll", async (c) => c.json(await blueskyOps.poll("page")));
  app.post(NS + "know", kernel, async (c) => {
    const body = await c.req.json();
    if (!Array.isArray(body.all) && (typeof body.address !== "string" || !body.address)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "address or all");
    return c.json(await blueskyOps.know(body));
  });
  app.get(NS + "status", async (c) => c.json(await blueskyOps.status()));
  return app;
}
// %%
bluesky_service = cloudflare.Service("bluesky", blueskyApp, {
  crons: ["* * * * *"],
  scheduled: () => blueskyOps.tick(),
  calls: ["com.lopecode.brain.lease.get"],
  methods: {
    "com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.send": { type: "procedure", allow: 'caller.kind in ["owner", "token"] || caller.id == "worker:brain-x-inbox"' },
    "com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.poll": { type: "procedure", who: "owner" },
    "com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.know": { type: "procedure", allow: 'caller.id == "kernel"' },
    "com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.room": { type: "procedure", allow: 'caller.id == "kernel"' },
    "com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.groups": { type: "query", who: "owner" },
    "com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.group": { type: "procedure", who: "owner" },
    "com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.start": { type: "procedure", who: "owner" },
    "com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.settings": { type: "procedure", who: "owner" },
    "com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.putRecord": { type: "procedure", allow: 'caller.session || (caller.worker == "brain-x-feed" && origin.kind == "owner")' },
    "com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.deleteRecord": { type: "procedure", allow: 'caller.session || (caller.worker == "brain-x-feed" && origin.kind == "owner")' },
    "com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.status": { type: "query", who: "owner" }
  }
})
// %%
bluesky_announce = {
  plugins.add("workers", bluesky_service, { invalidation });
  return "announced bluesky_service";
}
// %%
md`## Tests

The emitted Worker under \`simulate\`, against a stand-in for the directory, the account's PDS and the chat service. No test reaches Bluesky.`
// %%
// The account is did:plc:brain on https://pds.example. `events` is the chat log; `say(from, text)` adds a message to it.
blueskyRig = async ({ held = true, known = [], configured = true, owner = "did:plc:owner", pageSize = 50, allow = "following", credsMs = 0 } = {}) => {
  const jwt = (kind, n, exp) => `h.${btoa(JSON.stringify({ kind, n, exp: Math.floor(exp / 1000) }))}.s`;
  const net = { asked: [], sent: [], events: [], read: [], accepted: [], sessions: 0, refreshes: 0, live: 0, limit: 0, reset: null, password: "app-pass", declaration: allow === null ? null : { $type: "chat.bsky.actor.declaration", allowIncoming: allow }, groups: new Map(), past: new Set(), memberPage: 100, ttl: 7200000 };
  const state = { held };
  const no = (status, error, headers = {}) => Response.json({ error, message: error }, { status, headers });
  const issue = () => ({ accessJwt: jwt("access", ++net.live, Date.now() + net.ttl), refreshJwt: jwt("refresh", net.live, Date.now() + 86400000), did: "did:plc:brain", handle: "brain.example" });
  // A group is id -> { name, members: [did] }. As on the chat service, its convoView lists only some of its members.
  const profile = (did) => ({ did, handle: did.slice(8) + ".example", kind: { $type: "chat.bsky.actor.defs#" + (net.past.has(did) ? "pastGroupConvoMember" : "groupConvoMember"), role: "standard" } });
  const convoOf = (id) => {
    const g = net.groups.get(id);
    return g
      ? { id, rev: "r", muted: false, unreadCount: 0, members: [{ did: "did:plc:brain" }, ...g.members.slice(0, 1).map((did) => ({ did }))], kind: { $type: "chat.bsky.convo.defs#groupConvo", name: g.name, memberCount: g.members.length + 1 } }
      : { id, rev: "r", muted: false, unreadCount: 0, members: [{ did: "did:plc:brain" }, { did: id.slice(2) }], kind: { $type: "chat.bsky.convo.defs#directConvo" } };
  };
  const fetch = async (request) => {
    const u = new URL(request.url), nsid = u.pathname.replace("/xrpc/", ""), auth = request.headers.get("authorization") || "";
    const body = request.method === "POST" ? await request.json().catch(() => null) : null;
    net.asked.push({ host: u.hostname, nsid, proxy: request.headers.get("atproto-proxy"), body });
    if (u.hostname === "public.api.bsky.app") return Response.json({ did: "did:plc:brain" });
    if (u.hostname === "plc.directory") return Response.json({ id: "did:plc:brain", service: [{ id: "#atproto_pds", type: "AtprotoPersonalDataServer", serviceEndpoint: "https://pds.example" }] });
    if (u.hostname !== "pds.example") return no(404, "NotFound");
    if (net.limit > 0) return net.limit--, no(429, "RateLimitExceeded", net.reset ? { "ratelimit-reset": String(net.reset) } : {});
    if (nsid === "com.atproto.server.createSession") return body.identifier === "brain.example" && body.password === net.password ? (net.sessions++, Response.json(issue())) : no(401, "AuthenticationRequired");
    const token = (() => { try { return JSON.parse(atob(auth.replace("Bearer ", "").split(".")[1])); } catch { return null; } })();
    if (nsid === "com.atproto.server.refreshSession") return token && token.kind === "refresh" && token.n === net.live ? (net.refreshes++, Response.json(issue())) : no(400, "ExpiredToken");
    if (!token || token.kind !== "access") return no(401, "AuthenticationRequired");
    if (token.n !== net.live || token.exp * 1000 < Date.now()) return no(400, "ExpiredToken");
    if (nsid === "com.atproto.repo.getRecord") return net.declaration ? Response.json({ uri: "at://did:plc:brain/chat.bsky.actor.declaration/self", value: net.declaration }) : no(400, "RecordNotFound");
    if (nsid === "com.atproto.repo.putRecord" && body.collection !== "chat.bsky.actor.declaration") return (net.records ??= new Map()).set(body.collection + "/" + body.rkey, body), Response.json({ uri: `at://${body.repo}/${body.collection}/${body.rkey}`, cid: "c" + net.records.size });
    if (nsid === "com.atproto.repo.deleteRecord") return (net.records ??= new Map()).delete(body.collection + "/" + body.rkey), Response.json({});
    if (nsid === "com.atproto.repo.putRecord") return (net.declaration = body.record), Response.json({ uri: "at://x", cid: "c" });
    if (request.headers.get("atproto-proxy") !== "did:web:api.bsky.chat#bsky_chat") return no(501, "MethodNotImplemented");
    const name = nsid.replace("chat.bsky.convo.", "");
    if (name === "getLog") {
      const after = Number(u.searchParams.get("cursor") || 0), logs = net.events.filter((e) => e.n > after).slice(0, pageSize);
      return Response.json({ cursor: String(logs.length ? logs.at(-1).n : after), logs: logs.map((e) => e.log) });
    }
    if (name === "getConvo") return Response.json({ convo: convoOf(u.searchParams.get("convoId")) });
    if (name === "getConvoMembers") {
      const all = [profile("did:plc:brain"), ...net.groups.get(u.searchParams.get("convoId")).members.map(profile)], at = Number(u.searchParams.get("cursor") || 0);
      return Response.json({ members: all.slice(at, at + net.memberPage), ...(at + net.memberPage < all.length ? { cursor: String(at + net.memberPage) } : {}) });
    }
    if (name === "chat.bsky.group.createGroup") {
      const id = "g-" + body.name.toLowerCase();
      net.groups.set(id, { name: body.name, members: body.members });
      return Response.json({ convo: convoOf(id) });
    }
    if (name === "getConvoForMembers") return Response.json({ convo: convoOf("c-" + u.searchParams.get("members")) });
    if (name === "acceptConvo") return net.accepted.push(body.convoId), Response.json({ rev: "r" });
    if (name === "updateRead") return net.read.push(body.convoId), Response.json({ convo: convoOf(body.convoId) });
    if (name === "sendMessage") {
      if ([...new Intl.Segmenter().segment(body.message.text)].length > 1000) return no(400, "InvalidRequest");
      net.sent.push([body.convoId.slice(2), body.message.text, body.message.facets || null]);
      net.events.push({ n: net.events.length + 1, log: { $type: "chat.bsky.convo.defs#logCreateMessage", rev: "r", convoId: body.convoId, message: { $type: "chat.bsky.convo.defs#messageView", id: "out" + net.events.length, rev: "r", text: body.message.text, sender: { did: "did:plc:brain" }, sentAt: new Date().toISOString() } } });
      return Response.json({ id: "out", rev: "r", text: body.message.text, sender: { did: "did:plc:brain" }, sentAt: new Date().toISOString() });
    }
    return no(501, "MethodNotImplemented");
  };
  const sim = await simulate(bluesky_service, {
    rows: new Map(known.map((d) => ["known/" + d, { at: 1 }])),
    secrets: { BRAIN_KEY: "k" },
    // credsMs 0: a test changes a secret and reads it on the next poll.
    config: { host: "brain.example", owner, pollGapMs: 0, credsMs },
    fetch,
    core: async (request) => {
      const u = new URL(request.url), nsid = u.pathname.replace("/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.", "");
      if (nsid === "secret.get") {
        state.reads = (state.reads || 0) + 1;
        const name = u.searchParams.get("name"), value = sim.stored[name];
        return value === undefined ? Response.json({ error: "NotFound" }, { status: 404 }) : Response.json({ name, value });
      }
      if (nsid === "lease.get") return Response.json({ held: state.held });
      const data = await request.json();
      const seen = sim.inbox.find((e) => e.key === data.key);
      if (!seen) sim.inbox.push({ id: sim.inbox.length + 1, ...data });
      return Response.json({ id: seen ? seen.id : sim.inbox.length, duplicate: !!seen });
    }
  });
  sim.stored = configured ? { BLUESKY_HANDLE: "@brain.example", BLUESKY_APP_PASSWORD: "app-pass" } : {};
  let n = 0;
  const say = (from, text, { convo = "c-" + from, at = Date.now(), embed, facets, replyTo } = {}) => {
    const id = "m" + ++n;
    net.events.push({ n: net.events.length + 1, log: { $type: "chat.bsky.convo.defs#logCreateMessage", rev: "r", convoId: convo, message: { $type: "chat.bsky.convo.defs#messageView", id, rev: "r", text, sender: { did: from }, sentAt: new Date(at).toISOString(), ...(embed ? { embed } : {}), ...(facets ? { facets } : {}), ...(replyTo ? { replyTo } : {}) } } });
    return id;
  };
  // A message in a group that mentions the account, as a client writes it.
  const mention = (from, convo, text = "what is on today?") => say(from, "@brain.example " + text, { convo, facets: [{ index: { byteStart: 0, byteEnd: 14 }, features: [{ $type: "app.bsky.richtext.facet#mention", did: "did:plc:brain" }] }] });
  const log = (kind, convo) => net.events.push({ n: net.events.length + 1, log: { $type: "chat.bsky.convo.defs#log" + kind, rev: "r", convoId: convo } });
  const as = (who) => async (path, body) => {
    const r = await sim.fetch("https://brain.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.bluesky." + path, { method: body ? "POST" : "GET", body: body ? JSON.stringify(body) : undefined, headers: { "content-type": "application/json", "x-brain-caller": who } });
    return { status: r.status, data: await r.json() };
  };
  const owned = as("owner");
  return { sim, rows: sim.rows, net, state, say, mention, log, as, owned, kernel: as("kernel"), poll: async () => (await owned("poll", {})).data, tick: () => sim.scheduled(), bodies: () => sim.inbox.map((e) => [e.source, e.key, e.body.address, e.body.text]) };
}
// %%
test_bluesky_owner_message_in_and_reply_out = {
  const rig = await blueskyRig();
  const id = rig.say("did:plc:owner", "what is on today?");
  expect(await rig.poll()).toEqual({ configured: true, events: 1, taken: 1 });
  // The entry says which DID wrote. Whose message that makes it is the kernel's to say.
  expect(rig.sim.inbox.map((e) => [e.source, e.key, Object.keys(e.body).sort().join(), e.body.address, e.body.text])).toEqual([["bluesky", "bsky:" + id, "address,at,text", "did:plc:owner", "what is on today?"]]);
  expect(rig.net.accepted).toEqual(["c-did:plc:owner"]);
  // Signed in on the PDS the directory named, and every chat call was sent on to the chat service.
  const chat = rig.net.asked.filter((a) => a.nsid.startsWith("chat."));
  expect(rig.net.asked.slice(0, 3).map((a) => a.host + " " + a.nsid)).toEqual(["public.api.bsky.app com.atproto.identity.resolveHandle", "plc.directory /did:plc:brain", "pds.example com.atproto.server.createSession"]);
  expect(rig.net.asked[2].body).toEqual({ identifier: "brain.example", password: "app-pass" });
  expect([...new Set(chat.map((a) => a.host + " " + a.proxy))]).toEqual(["pds.example did:web:api.bsky.chat#bsky_chat"]);
  // The reply path: inbox.reply calls bluesky.send as brain-x-inbox with the entry's address.
  expect((await rig.as("worker:brain-x-inbox")("send", { to: "did:plc:owner", text: "Nothing. See https://brain.example/today." })).data).toEqual({ sent: true });
  expect(rig.net.sent).toEqual([["did:plc:owner", "Nothing. See https://brain.example/today.", [{ index: { byteStart: 13, byteEnd: 40 }, features: [{ $type: "app.bsky.richtext.facet#link", uri: "https://brain.example/today" }] }]]]);
  expect(rig.net.read).toEqual(["c-did:plc:owner"]);
  // Its own reply comes back in the log and is not taken for a message.
  expect(await rig.poll()).toEqual({ configured: true, events: 1, taken: 0 });
  expect(rig.sim.inbox.length).toBe(1);
  return "1 entry, 1 reply, 1 read mark";
}
// %%
test_bluesky_a_person_is_served_and_a_stranger_is_told_once = {
  const rig = await blueskyRig();
  rig.say("did:plc:ada", "hello");
  rig.say("did:plc:ada", "hello?");
  await rig.poll();
  expect(rig.sim.inbox.length).toBe(0);
  expect(rig.net.sent).toEqual([["did:plc:ada", "This account answers people its owner has added, and did:plc:ada is not one of them.", null]]);
  expect(rig.net.accepted).toEqual([]);
  // Nobody but the kernel says who is known.
  for (const who of ["owner", "worker:brain-x-evil", "worker:brain-x-inbox", "did:plc:ada"]) expect([who, (await rig.as(who)("know", { address: "did:plc:ada" })).status]).toEqual([who, 401]);
  expect((await rig.kernel("know", { address: "did:plc:ada" })).data).toEqual({ known: true });
  const id = rig.say("did:plc:ada", "now?");
  await rig.poll();
  expect(rig.bodies()).toEqual([["bluesky", "bsky:" + id, "did:plc:ada", "now?"]]);
  expect((await rig.owned("send", { to: "did:plc:ada", text: "yes" })).data).toEqual({ sent: true });
  // Forgotten, she is a stranger again, and is not told a second time within the hour.
  await rig.kernel("know", { address: "did:plc:ada", forget: true });
  rig.say("did:plc:ada", "still here?");
  await rig.poll();
  expect(rig.sim.inbox.length).toBe(1);
  expect(rig.net.sent.length).toBe(2);
  expect((await rig.owned("send", { to: "did:plc:ada", text: "hi" })).status).toBe(403);
  rig.rows.set("asked/did:plc:ada", Date.now() - 3600001);
  rig.say("did:plc:ada", "hello again");
  await rig.poll();
  expect(rig.net.sent.length).toBe(3);
  // The whole set at once, as the kernel sends it when People changes.
  expect((await rig.kernel("know", { all: ["did:plc:bo", "did:plc:cy"] })).data).toEqual({ known: 2 });
  expect([...rig.rows.keys()].filter((k) => k.startsWith("known/"))).toEqual(["known/did:plc:bo", "known/did:plc:cy"]);
  return "stranger: 2 answers for 4 messages over an hour; person: 1 entry";
}
